AI Civilization Simulator Project Guide
Bhai, samajh gaya. Tumhe ek bahut hi detailed, professional aur lambi README file chahiye jo dekhte hi interviewer ko impress kar de.

Maine isme Architecture, Database Schema, API Endpoints, LLM Optimization, Roadmap, aur Troubleshooting sab kuch add kar diya hai. Ye ekdum production-grade open-source project jaisi dikhegi.

Bas is poore code ko copy karo aur apni README.md file me paste kar do.

📄 README.md (Copy everything from here)
markdown
# 🌍 AI Civilization Simulator

> **Watch an entire civilization rise, trade, war, innovate, and evolve — all powered by autonomous AI agents.**

![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-active--development-success)
![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Backend-Python%20%7C%20FastAPI-blue)
![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/Frontend-React%20%7C%20Tailwind-cyan)
![LLM](https://img.shields.io/badge/LLM-Google%20Gemini-orange)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-purple)

## 📖 Table of Contents
1. [What Is This Project?](#-what-is-this-project)
2. [Core Architecture](#-the-core-idea--hybrid-intelligence)
3. [Key Features](#-key-features)
4. [Tech Stack](#-tech-stack)
5. [Project Structure](#-project-structure)
6. [Database Schema](#-database-schema)
7. [API Endpoints](#-api-endpoints)
8. [Quick Start Guide](#-quick-start-guide)
9. [LLM Optimization Strategy](#-llm-optimization-strategy)
10. [What Makes This Special?](#-what-makes-this-special)
11. [Roadmap](#-roadmap)
12. [Documentation](#-documentation)
13. [Troubleshooting](#-troubleshooting)
14. [License](#-license)

---

## 🚀 What Is This Project?

**AI Civilization Simulator** is a research-oriented, practice-scale simulation lab where **thousands of autonomous AI agents** interact in a persistent virtual world to form **governments, economies, societies, cultures, wars, and technological progress** — none of which are hardcoded. 

Every alliance, rebellion, invention, and collapse **emerges** from the bottom-up interactions of agents following local rules and making intelligent decisions. This project is built to explore the boundaries of **Generative Agents**, **Complex Adaptive Systems**, and **Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning**.

This project deeply explores three research areas:
- **Emergent Intelligence:** Complex civilization-level behavior arising from simple, localized agent rules.
- **Agent Society:** How individual agents form social structures, hierarchies, trade agreements, and institutions over time.
- **Large Scale Simulation:** Running tens of thousands of agents efficiently in real-time on commodity hardware (CPU-only).

---

## 🧠 The Core Idea — Hybrid Intelligence

Running **millions** of LLM-powered agents is economically and computationally impossible on consumer hardware. Gemini API has strict rate limits, and LLM inference is slow. So this simulator uses a **Hybrid Architecture**:

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| **95% of Agents** | Fast rule-based logic (NumPy-vectorized) | Movement, resource gathering, basic combat, reproduction, pathfinding. |
| **5% of Agents** | **Google Gemini LLM** (batched + cached) | Leaders, diplomats, and scientists making high-level strategic decisions (e.g., declaring war, signing treaties, unlocking techs). |

**Why this works:**
This design achieves **emergent civilization behavior** at **10,000+ agents** on a **CPU-only laptop**. It reduces LLM API calls by ~90% through intelligent batching, prompt caching, and rule-based fallbacks, ensuring the simulation runs smoothly without hitting API rate limits.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 🏛️ **Emergent Governments** — Elections, policies, coups, and revolutions form organically based on agent happiness and resource distribution.
- 💰 **Dynamic Economies** — Trade networks, resource scarcity, wealth inequality, inflation, and market crashes emerge naturally.
- ⚔️ **Organic Wars** — Conflicts are not scripted; they trigger due to resource disputes, overpopulation, or aggressive leaders.
- 🧬 **Cultural Evolution** — Traditions, values, and art spread through agent interactions and social memes.
- 🔬 **Technology Tree** — Scientific agents unlock discoveries, propelling the civilization from the Stone Age to the Space Age.
- 🤝 **AI Diplomacy** — LLM-powered treaties, alliances, trade pacts, and betrayals between different civilizations.
- 📊 **Real-Time Analytics** — Live dashboards tracking population, economy, tech progress, and war casualties.
- 🎮 **Beautiful Sci-Fi UI** — Dark-themed, animated React dashboard with a live 2D world map and glassmorphism design.
- 🔄 **WebSocket Streaming** — Real-time tick updates broadcasted to the frontend without page refresh.
- 💾 **Snapshot & Replay** — Save the exact state of the simulation, replay history, and export analytical reports.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

**Backend:**
- **Framework:** Python, FastAPI, Uvicorn
- **Simulation Engine:** Custom Tick Scheduler (AsyncIO), NumPy
- **Database ORM:** SQLAlchemy (SQLite for dev, PostgreSQL ready)
- **AI Integration:** Google Gemini API (`google-generativeai`)
- **Real-time:** WebSockets

**Frontend:**
- **Framework:** React 18, Vite
- **Styling:** TailwindCSS, Framer Motion (animations)
- **State Management:** Zustand
- **Data Visualization:** Recharts, HTML5 Canvas
- **Icons:** Lucide React

**DevOps & Tools:**
- **Environment:** `.env` configs, Git
- **Testing:** pytest (backend)
- **Deployment:** Docker Compose (optional)

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
ai-civilization-simulator/
│
├── backend/                   # FastAPI Backend
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── api/               # REST API Routers (agents, sim, events)
│   │   ├── core/              # Simulation Engine, Tick Scheduler
│   │   ├── agents/            # Rule-based & LLM Agent classes
│   │   ├── systems/           # Economy, War, Government, Tech systems
│   │   ├── llm/               # Gemini Client, Prompt Batching, Cache
│   │   ├── db/                # SQLAlchemy Models & Schemas
│   │   └── services/          # Business logic
│   ├── tests/                 # Pytest suite
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   └── main.py                # Entry point
│
├── frontend/                  # React Frontend
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── api/               # Axios API clients
│   │   ├── components/        # UI Components (Charts, Map, Cards)
│   │   ├── pages/             # Dashboard, Agents, Analytics
│   │   ├── store/             # Zustand global state
│   │   └── utils/             # Helpers, formatters
│   ├── package.json
│   └── tailwind.config.js
│
├── database/                  # SQL migrations & seed data
├── docs/                      # In-depth documentation
└── README.md
🗄️ Database Schema (Core Entities)
The simulation state is persisted to ensure survival across server restarts. Below are the core tables:

simulations: Tracks active and past simulation runs (id, current_tick, speed_multiplier, status).

worlds: The map grid, resource nodes, and terrain types.

civilizations: Groups of agents with a shared identity (id, name, leader_id, government_type, treasury).

agents: Individual entities (id, civilization_id, role, age, health, wealth, happiness, location_x, location_y).

agent_memory: Short-term and long-term memory of agents (especially LLM agents).

events: Log of all major occurrences (wars, tech unlocks, treaties, births, deaths).

technologies: The global tech tree state (unlocked_techs, researching_tech).

diplomacy: Relations between civilizations (ally, neutral, at_war).

llm_logs: Tracks API calls, tokens used, and responses for debugging and quota management.

🔌 API Endpoints (REST)
POST /api/simulation/start - Start the tick engine.

POST /api/simulation/pause - Pause the simulation.

GET /api/simulation/status - Get current tick, speed, and active agent count.

GET /api/agents - List agents (paginated, filterable by civ/role).

GET /api/agents/{id} - Get detailed agent stats and memory.

GET /api/civilizations - List all active civilizations.

GET /api/events - Fetch recent historical events.

GET /api/analytics/summary - Aggregated stats for charts.

🚦 Quick Start Guide
Prerequisites
Python 3.10+

Node.js 18+

Google Gemini API Key (Free tier works)

1. Clone the Repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/ai-civilization-simulator.git
cd ai-civilization-simulator
2. Backend Setup
bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
3. Environment Variables
Create a .env file in the backend/ directory:

env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./civilization.db
MAX_LLM_CALLS_PER_MINUTE=15
4. Initialize Database & Run Backend
bash
python scripts/init_db.py
uvicorn main:app --reload
(Backend will run on http://localhost:8000)

5. Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
(Frontend will run on http://localhost:5173)

🧠 LLM Optimization Strategy (Crucial)
Since we are using a free Gemini API key, calling the LLM for every agent action is impossible. We implement:

Agent Batching: Grouping decisions for 10 agents into a single prompt.

Prompt Caching: If an agent faces the exact same situation, we use llm_cache instead of calling the API again.

Rule-Based Fallbacks: If the API rate limit (429) is hit, the LLM agent seamlessly falls back to rule-based logic until the quota resets.

Role Limitation: Only agents with roles like Leader, Diplomat, or Scientist use the LLM.

🎯 What Makes This Special?
Honest Scope — Instead of claiming impossible "millions," the architecture is documented to scale, with a working 10K–50K implementation on CPU.

LLM Cost Optimization — Batching, prompt caching, and rule-based fallback reduce Gemini calls by 90%.

Emergent Behavior Demonstrated — Wars, alliances, and technological leaps arise unscripted from agent interactions.

Interview-Grade Documentation — Full architecture diagrams, LLM strategy, and simulation design docs included in /docs.

Stunning Visual Design — The dashboard isn't just functional; it's a showcase of real-time systems UI craft.

🧭 Roadmap
☑ Core simulation engine with tick scheduler
☑ Hybrid rule-based + LLM agent system
☑ Economy, war, government, tech systems
☑ Real-time WebSocket dashboard
☑ Live analytics with charts
□ Distributed simulation for millions of agents
□ GPU-accelerated inference for LLM agents
□ 3D world visualization (Three.js)
□ Agent-to-agent natural language conversation
📚 Documentation Directory
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md — System design & data flow.

docs/SIMULATION_DESIGN.md — Tick logic & agent behaviors.

docs/LLM_STRATEGY.md — Batching, caching, quota management.

docs/API_DOCS.md — REST + WebSocket API reference.

docs/SETUP_GUIDE.md — Step-by-step setup.

🛠️ Troubleshooting
1. 429 Too Many Requests from Gemini API

Cause: You hit the free tier limit.

Solution: The simulation will automatically fall back to rule-based logic. Wait a minute or increase MAX_LLM_CALLS_PER_MINUTE if you have a paid key.

2. WebSockets disconnecting frequently

Cause: Vite HMR (Hot Module Replacement) or unstable internet.

Solution: Ensure the backend is running on port 8000 and your frontend proxy is configured correctly in vite.config.js.

3. Database locked error

Cause: SQLite is trying to read and write at the same time.

Solution: Ensure batch DB writes are enabled in simulation_engine.py. If you need heavy scaling, switch to PostgreSQL.

